Day 15 — Pointers basics

Learn: Memory addresses, &, *, pointer declaration, dereferencing, NULL.

Practice:
- Print the address of a variable.
- Access a value using a pointer.
- Swap two numbers using pointers.
- Modify a variable through a function using a pointer.



16

Day 16 — Advanced pointers

Learn: Pointer arithmetic, pointers and arrays, pointers and strings, double pointers (int **), array of pointers, pointer to array.

Practice:
- Traverse an array using a pointer.
- Reverse an array using pointers.
- Access a string using a pointer.
- Use a pointer to pointer to modify a variable.
- Understand the difference between int *p[5] and int (*p)[5].



17

Day 17 — Dynamic memory allocation

Learn: Stack versus heap, malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), free(), memory leaks, dangling pointers.

Practice:
- Allocate an integer dynamically.
- Create an array whose size is entered by the user.
- Resize an array using realloc().
- Find the sum of dynamically allocated array elements.
- Free all allocated memory safely.



18

Day 18 — Structures, unions and enums

Learn: struct, nested structures, arrays of structures, union, enum, typedef, . and ->.

Practice:
- Store student details using a structure.
- Create an array of student records.
- Make an employee record system.
- Compare the memory usage of a structure and a union.
- Use an enum for menu choices or device states.



19

Day 19 — File handling

Learn: FILE *, fopen(), fclose(), fprintf(), fscanf(), fgets(), fputs(), fread(), fwrite(), file modes, EOF.

Practice:
- Write text into a file.
- Read and display file contents.
- Append new records.
- Count lines and words in a file.
- Save and retrieve student records.



20

Day 20 — Bitwise operators

Learn: &, |, ^, ~, <<, >>, bit masks, setting, clearing, toggling, and testing bits.

Practice:
- Check whether a number is odd or even using a bitwise operator.
- Set a particular bit.
- Clear a particular bit.
- Toggle a particular bit.
- Check whether a particular bit is set.
Important for ECE: These concepts are useful in register manipulation and embedded systems.



21

Day 21 — Preprocessor and C program organization

Learn: #include, #define, macros, conditional compilation (#if, #ifdef, #ifndef), header guards, separate source and header files, static, const, volatile, sizeof.

Practice:
- Create macros for square and maximum of two values.
- Make your own header file.
- Split a calculator into .c and .h files.
- Use conditional compilation to enable debugging output.
- Compare const pointers and pointers to const data.